<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mukunda Sen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mukunda Sen was a ruler of the Sen dynasty of Palpa in the hills of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> in the 16th century. He is said to have campaigned as far as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a>. After his death his realm was divided among his heirs, giving rise to separate kingdoms such as Palpa and Tanahun.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mukunda-sen.jpg" alt="Mukunda Sen" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_invading_Mukunda_Sen,_a_king_of_Palpa.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
